cdjot-specific tests: bugs found via corpus comparison against JS djot,
plus regression tests for spec-correct behavior that JS djot gets wrong.

Verbatim space stripping applies regardless of delimiter length.
The spec says: "If the content starts or ends with a backtick character,
a single space is removed between the opening or closing backticks and
the content."

```
`` `foo` ``
.
<p><code>`foo`</code></p>
```

URL line continuation: "the line breaks and any leading and trailing
space is ignored, and the lines are concatenated together."

```
[link](http://example.com?n=123
    456)
.
<p><a href="http://example.com?n=123456">link</a></p>
```

Emphasis precedence: "When there are multiple openers that might be
matched with a given closer, the closest one is used."

```
*not strong *strong*
.
<p>*not strong <strong>strong</strong></p>
```

Nested emphasis: "Emphasis can be nested."

```
__emphasis inside_ emphasis_
.
<p><em><em>emphasis inside</em> emphasis</em></p>
```

Loose list: when a list has blank lines (making it loose), ALL
items should be wrapped in <p>, not just items with continuation.

```
- a
- b
- c

  more

- d
.
<ul>
<li>
<p>a</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>b</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>c</p>
<p>more</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>d</p>
</li>
</ul>
```

Inline comments: "Material between two % characters in an attribute
will be ignored and treated as a comment."

```
Hello {% comment %} world
.
<p>Hello  world</p>
```

Image with inline attributes: attributes after ![alt](src){attrs}
should go on the <img> tag, not wrap in a <span>.

```
![alt](img.jpg){.photo}
.
<p><img alt="alt" src="img.jpg" class="photo"></p>
```

Regression tests: these verify spec-correct behavior where the
djot.js npm release (v0.3.2) diverged. Already fixed upstream.

Emphasis delimiters inside link URLs don't close emphasis:

```
*[closed](hello*)
.
<p>*<a href="hello*">closed</a></p>
```

```
_[link](http://example.com?foo_bar=1), more text_
.
<p><em><a href="http://example.com?foo_bar=1">link</a>, more text</em></p>
```

Block attributes require no blank line before the block:

```
{#id .class}

A paragraph
.
<p>A paragraph</p>
```

Heading auto-ID excludes footnote reference text (spec explicitly
states: "# Introduction[^1] generates the identifier Introduction,
not Introduction1"):

```
# Introduction[^1]

[^1]: A note.
.
<section id="Introduction">
<h1>Introduction<a id="fnref1" href="#fn1" role="doc-noteref"><sup>1</sup></a></h1>
</section>
<section role="doc-endnotes">
<hr>
<ol>
<li id="fn1">
<p>A note.<a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩︎</a></p>
</li>
</ol>
</section>
```

Different bullet markers create separate lists:

```
- [ ] foo
+ [ ] bar
* [ ] baz
.
<ul class="task-list">
<li>
<input disabled="" type="checkbox"/>
foo
</li>
</ul>
<ul class="task-list">
<li>
<input disabled="" type="checkbox"/>
bar
</li>
</ul>
<ul class="task-list">
<li>
<input disabled="" type="checkbox"/>
baz
</li>
</ul>
```

Inline attributes on links: {key=val}, {.class}, {#id} after
[text](url) should attach to the <a> element.

```
[a](b){rel=me}
.
<p><a href="b" rel="me">a</a></p>
```

```
[a](b){rel="me"}
.
<p><a href="b" rel="me">a</a></p>
```

```
[a](b){.cls #id}
.
<p><a href="b" id="id" class="cls">a</a></p>
```

Inline attributes on emphasis should attach to the element,
not wrap in a <span>.

```
_emph_{.a}
.
<p><em class="a">emph</em></p>
```

```
*strong*{.a}
.
<p><strong class="a">strong</strong></p>
```

Inline attributes on sub/superscript:

```
~sub~{.a}
.
<p><sub class="a">sub</sub></p>
```

```
^sup^{.a}
.
<p><sup class="a">sup</sup></p>
```

Inline attributes on insert/delete/mark:

```
{+ins+}{.a}
.
<p><ins class="a">ins</ins></p>
```

```
{-del-}{.a}
.
<p><del class="a">del</del></p>
```

```
{=mark=}{.a}
.
<p><mark class="a">mark</mark></p>
```

Inline attributes on code spans:

```
`code`{.a}
.
<p><code class="a">code</code></p>
```

```
`code`{key="value"}
.
<p><code key="value">code</code></p>
```

Inline attributes on autolinks:

```
<https://example.com>{.a}
.
<p><a href="https://example.com" class="a">https://example.com</a></p>
```

```
<https://example.com>{#id .cls}
.
<p><a href="https://example.com" id="id" class="cls">https://example.com</a></p>
```

Combined inline attributes with id, class, and key=val:

```
_emph_{#id .cls key=val}
.
<p><em id="id" class="cls" key="val">emph</em></p>
```

Tight/loose list detection must not look past the end of the list.
A later loose list in the same document should not cause an earlier
tight list to be rendered as loose.

```
- a
- b

text

- x

- y
.
<ul>
<li>
a
</li>
<li>
b
</li>
</ul>
<p>text</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>x</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>y</p>
</li>
</ul>
```

Table separator rows must have no leading space after the opening |.
`| --- | --- |` is not a separator because the first cell starts with
a space. This matches djot.js behavior.

```
| a | b |
| --- | --- |
| c | d |
.
<table>
<tr>
<td>a</td>
<td>b</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>—</td>
<td>—</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>c</td>
<td>d</td>
</tr>
</table>
```

No leading space: it IS a separator.

```
| a | b |
|---|---|
| c | d |
.
<table>
<tr>
<th>a</th>
<th>b</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>c</td>
<td>d</td>
</tr>
</table>
```

Block attributes preceding a definition list should attach to
the <dl>, not leak into the first <dd>'s content.

```
{variant=Simple}
: term

  definition
.
<dl variant="Simple">
<dt>term</dt>
<dd>
<p>definition</p>
</dd>
</dl>
```

Multi-line {% ... %} block comments require continuation lines to
be indented. Without indentation, it's a regular paragraph.

```
{%
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2025
%}

Hello.
.
<p>{%
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2025
%}</p>
<p>Hello.</p>
```

With indented continuation, it's a valid block comment.

```
{%
  SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2025
  %}

Hello.
.
<p>Hello.</p>
```

Reference links inside image alt text should be resolved to their
label text, not emitted literally.

```
[foo]: http://example.com/foo

![alt with [foo][] text](/img.png)
.
<p><img alt="alt with foo text" src="/img.png"></p>
```

```
[foo]: http://example.com/foo

![alt [foo][foo] here](/img.png)
.
<p><img alt="alt foo here" src="/img.png"></p>
```
